[{:db/id "q-334544/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "5916280f-0472-568a-8079-bf285cc81e4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334544/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "b6b93d36-6bac-58a7-a664-69247c11a284" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334544/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "6dc36703-75eb-5afe-859b-2ce2866899f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334544/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "4983bc87-8140-5aa7-bda9-5c0258088161" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334544/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "7f29c5fd-4a78-5841-8d8e-796392a8974c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334544/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "58b9225f-157c-553b-be20-43c7488467c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-334544/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-334544/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-334544/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-334544/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-334544/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-334544/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334544" :question/id #uuid "500e48c1-7345-566d-9368-b7d69cfccd17" :question/math-academy-id "q-334544" :question/problem "A numerical method is used to approximate the solution to an initial value problem.\n\n- With step size $Δx=0.18,$ the observed global truncation error is $e(0.18)=0.740.$\n\n- With step size $Δx=0.06,$ the observed global truncation error is $e(0.06)=0.090.$\n\nUse this data to estimate the order of the numerical method." :question/worked-solution "A numerical method has order $p$ if $p$ is the largest positive integer such that the global truncation error (GTE) satisfies\n\n$$\ne(Δx)=O\\,((Δx)^{p})\\,\\text{as}\\,Δx\\to 0.\n$$\n\nThe order describes how fast errors shrink as $Δx$ decreases.\n\nIn other words, a numerical method has order $p$ if, for sufficiently small step sizes, reducing the step size by a factor of $k$ reduces the GTE by a factor of approximately ${k}^{p}.$\n\nIn our case, the step size decreases from $0.18$ to $0.06.$ So, it reduces by a factor of\n\n$$\nk=\\frac{0.18}{0.06}=3.\n$$\n\nAs a result, for a numerical method of order $p,$ the GTE should decrease by a factor of approximately\n\n$$\n{k}^{p}={3}^{p}.\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, the GTE actually decreases from $0.740$ to $0.090.$ So, it reduces by a factor of\n\n$$\n\\frac{0.740}{0.090}=8.222….\n$$\n\nComparing the two scale factors for the GTE, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{p} & ≈8.222… \\\\ p & ≈{log}_{3}⁡(8.222…) \\\\ p & ≈1.917….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, rounding to the nearest integer, the approximate order of the method is $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-334544/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "48cd517d-be8a-5dc2-91af-fbd19231363c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334544"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-334567/field-1/bc49e1fc31c7a3dc56193bd2b75162de77c86574fd1d6e1b702acbacd4225a1c" :answer/id #uuid "1f98e1ad-c6f2-5db2-8696-cd2f0ea4bcc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.181" :db/ensure [:answer/v