857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "be2e4a2a-83e5-51f0-9d89-3195c29a97c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334567/field-4/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "0e5dc91a-ab23-5955-9902-a2c5525c00f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334567/field-4/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "9da66781-8ec8-5fc6-bc9f-d87b0740392e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334567/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "d57cac1e-3d10-5339-bca7-4315cd2f49f9" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-334567/field-4/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-334567/field-4/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-334567/field-4/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-334567/field-4/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-334567/field-4/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-334567/field-4/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334567" :question/id #uuid "db1b2cc2-9ed0-52dd-b570-f28962fe5ef0" :question/math-academy-id "q-334567" :question/problem "The global truncation error (GTE) of a numerical method with step size $Δx$ is\n\n$$\ne(Δx)=2(Δx)^{4}-(Δx)^{5}.\n$$\n\nComplete the following sentences.$\\,$ With step size $Δx=0.6,$ the global truncation error is $≈$\n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ With step size $Δx=0.2,$ the global truncation error is $≈$\n{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Decreasing from $Δx=0.6$ to $Δx=0.2,$ the GTE is reduced by a factor of $≈$\n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ According to this data, the order of the method is approximately\n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "A numerical method has order $p$ if $p$ is the largest positive integer such that the global truncation error (GTE) satisfies\n\n$$\ne(Δx)=O\\,((Δx)^{p})\\,\\text{as}\\,Δx\\to 0.\n$$\n\nThe order describes how fast errors shrink as $Δx$ decreases.\n\nIn other words, a numerical method has order $p$ if, for sufficiently small step sizes, reducing the step size by a factor of $k$ reduces the GTE by a factor of approximately ${k}^{p}.$\n\nFirst, we compute the GTE for the given step sizes:\n\n- With step size $Δx=0.6,$ the GTE is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}e(0.6) & =2(0.6)^{4}-(0.6)^{5} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0.129\\,6-1\\cdot 0.077\\,76 \\\\  & =0.259\\,2-0.077\\,76 \\\\  & =0.181\\,44 \\\\  & ≈0.181.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- With step size $Δx=0.2,$ the GTE is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}e(0.2) & =2(0.2)^{4}-(0.2)^{5} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0.001\\,6-1\\cdot 0.000\\,32 \\\\  & =0.003\\,2-0.000\\,32 \\\\  & =0.002\\,88 \\\\  & ≈0.003.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we determine the order by comparing the errors. The step size decreases from $0.6$ to $0.2.$ So, it reduces by a factor of\n\n$$\nk=\\frac{0.6}{0.2}=3.\n$$\n\nAs a result, for a numerical method of order $p,$ the GTE should decrease by a factor of approximately\n\n$$\n{k}^{p}={3}^{p}.\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, the GTE actually decreases from $0.181\\,44$ to $0.002\\,88.$ So, it reduces by a factor of\n\n$$\n\\frac{0.181\\,44}{0.002\\,88}=63≈63.000.\n$$\n\nComparing the two scale factors for the GTE, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{p} & ≈63 \\\\ p & ≈{log}_{3}⁡(63) \\\\ p & ≈3.771….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, rounding to the nearest integer, the estimated order of the method is\n$4.$\n\nIndeed, this coincides with the definition of the order from the expression for the GTE:\n\n$$\ne(Δx)=2(Δx)^{4}-(Δx)^{5}\\,⇒\\,e(Δx)=O\\,((Δx)^{4})\\,\\text{as}\\,Δx\\to 0.\n$$\n\nHence, the order of the method is $4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-334567/field-1" "q-334567/field-2" "q-334567/field-3" "q-334567/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "48cd517d-be8a-5dc2-91af-fbd19231363c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334567"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-334569/field-1/93e09a05b80f698d016c0968c3fb4ae5bed9fd483754e17f516e5afaf4569f03" :answer/id #uuid "87d73130-c059-5091-a54c-8f869f5cc406" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.008" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334569/field-1/bc54ac80ead628012bc107ff401ceb38bf2d3595cc00b779dc63d086966009d7" :answer/id #uuid "9ff14842-247e-5a10-90ad-5926a5091567" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.321" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334569/field-1/4736cff726cb18beccbbe65c042c6022b5976f7c0c41f076f9da2a3f78d92fd6" :answer/id #uuid "f80a6bfa-1d70-5a8b-8aa7-ba429bbfcccf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.032" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334569/field-1/08da2abbdc7b4530519abeca6487ec34da284a62a989a5f1af3d42f5171b5d2f" :answer/id #uuid "869b5c1a-98c2-59ef-854d-79794d318318" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.207" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334569/field-1/69057a73aa8ac9b7be0670c894335bba92530ce2f5ae5dd5b72c07abe26c8c64" :answer/id #uuid "f4539f9b-d16b-5117-ae70-a49e4b3a7b0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.514" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334569/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e14ceace-04ce-5f64-bd27-04a958bbad06" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-334569/field-1/4736cff726cb18beccbbe65c042c6022b5976f7c0c41f076f9da2a3f78d92fd6" :answer-field/choices ["q-334569/field-1/93e09a05b80f698d016c0968c3fb4ae5bed9fd483754e17f516e5afaf4569f03" "q-334569/field-1/bc54ac80ead628012bc107ff401ceb38bf2d3595cc00b779dc63d086966009d7" "q-334569/field-1/4736cff726cb18beccbbe65c042c6022b5976f7c0c41f076f9da2a3f78d92fd6" "q-334569/field-1/08d